# Everything the extension does not need at runtime. The Marketplace package
# should be what VS Code loads — themes, the bundled Core, the preview adapter —
# not the machinery used to produce them.
#
# palettes/ is not machinery: extension.js reads palettes/<id>.json at render
# time to give the preview the colours of whichever JSRay theme is active.
# Excluding it did nothing in development, where the folder is simply there,
# and shipped a package where picking Ember gave an Ember editor beside a
# Default-coloured preview.
node_modules/**
package-lock.json
.vscode/**
.vscode-test/**
.vscode-test-profile/**
tests/**
tools/**
docker-compose.yml
.github/**
.gitignore
.vscodeignore
CONTRIBUTING.md
CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md
SECURITY.md
version.json
*.vsix
